{
  "solution": "Summary of the existence part\n\n* \\(k=0\\) – vertical lines.  \n* \\(k=1\\) – one sunny line \\(y=x\\) plus \\(n-1\\) non‑sunny lines as in §5.2.1.  \n* \\(k=n\\) – the \\(n\\) sunny lines of §5.2.2.  \n* For every \\(k\\) with \\(3\\le k\\le n-1\\) – the mixed construction of §5.2.3.\n\nThus for every \\(n\\ge3\\) and every integer \\(k\\) with \\(k\\neq2\\) and\n\\(0\\le k\\le n\\) there exists a required configuration.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n### 5.4  Completion of the proof\n\nCombining the impossibility of \\(k=2\\) (Section 5.1) with the explicit\nconstructions for all other admissible values (Section 5.2) we obtain the\ncharacterisation announced in Section 4.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{For every }n\\ge3,\\;\n       \\{k\\mid\\text{a configuration exists}\\}\n       =\\{0,1\\}\\cup\\{k\\mid 3\\le k\\le n\\}.}\n\\]",
